==English==

===Etymology 1===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*terh₂-}}
{{ety|en|:inh|enm:thurgh|tree=1}}
From {{inh|en|enm|thurgh}}, {{m|enm|thrugh}}, {{m|enm|thruch}}, {{m|enm|thruh}}, [[metathetic]] variants of {{m|enm|thurgh}}, {{m|enm|thurh}}, from {{inh|en|ang|þurh}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*þurhw||through}}, from {{inh|en|ine-pro|*tr̥h₂kʷe}}, suffixed zero-grade  from {{m|ine-pro|*terh₂-||to pass through}} + {{m|ine-pro|*-kʷe||and}}. 
{{col-top|2|cog}}
Cognate with {{cog|frr|döör||through}}, {{cog|stq|truch||through}}, {{cog|fy|troch||through}}, {{cog|nl|door||through}}, {{cog|de|durch||through}}, {{cog|lb|duerch||through}}, {{cog|vls|deur||through}}, {{cog|yi|דורך||through}}, {{cog|got|𐌸𐌰𐌹𐍂𐌷||through}}, {{cog|la|trans||across, over, through}}, {{cog|sq|tërthor||through, around}}, {{cog|cy|tra||through}}. See also [[thorough]].
